                            What is encapsulation?

                        </button>

                    </h2>

                    <div id="encapsulationQuestionOne"
                         class="accordion-collapse collapse"
                         data-bs-parent="#encapsulationQuestions">

                        <div class="accordion-body">

                            Encapsulation combines data and behavior inside a
                            class while controlling access to the object's
                            internal state.

                        </div>

                    </div>

                </div>


                <div class="accordion-item">

                    <h2 class="accordion-header">

                        <button class="accordion-button collapsed"
                                type="button"
                                data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                                data-bs-target="#encapsulationQuestionTwo">

                            Why are fields commonly declared private?

                        </button>

                    </h2>

                    <div id="encapsulationQuestionTwo"
                         class="accordion-collapse collapse"
                         data-bs-parent="#encapsulationQuestions">

                        <div class="accordion-body">

                            Private fields prevent unrelated code from
                            directly modifying internal state and allow the
                            class to control access.

                        </div>

                    </div>

                </div>


                <div class="accordion-item">

                    <h2 class="accordion-header">

                        <button class="accordion-button collapsed"
                                type="button"
                                data-bs-toggle="collapse"
